"""
Project 2: Volatility Modeling & Options Analytics

Black-Scholes with dividend yield + Greeks + implied volatility solver,
extended with:
  1. GARCH(1,1) vs. naive historical volatility forecasting, evaluated
     walk-forward and compared via a Diebold-Mariano test.
  2. Implied volatility smile/skew extraction from a real market option
     chain, with a regression test for whether the smile/skew is
     statistically significant (i.e., whether Black-Scholes' constant-
     volatility assumption is empirically violated).
  3. A paired test comparing option-pricing accuracy (GARCH-vol vs.
     historical-vol as the BS input) against real market prices.

Run locally (needs internet access for yfinance to pull the underlying's
price history; the option chain for the smile section needs to come from
a source that actually publishes NSE option data -- see NOTE in section D).
"""

